      "literal_utf8": "{\n  \"format\": \"jitml-phase278-independent-principal-four-scope-assessment-v1\",\n  \"reviewer\": \"Codex /root/cpu55_terminal_failure_review\",\n  \"reviewed_utc\": \"2026-10-28T17:59:35.933126+00:00\",\n  \"reviewer_role_and_authorship\": \"I am the actual principal criterion assessor, distinct from draft/compatibility-note author /root/phase278_status_review, peer /root/cpu55_post_preservation_review and mechanical operator Root. Earlier I authored two focused budget cases and test-only historical fixture corrections in Main/SupervisedCohortPlan, plus disabled native helper/caller/adopter derivatives. Root authored the production ProductBudget patch. I did not author these criterion drafts or run compilation/gates/export/training/materialization. This is independent criterion reasoning with those roles disclosed, not author-independent implementation approval.\",\n  \"operator_delegation\": \"Legacy --root-assessment carries this actual Terminal principal FILE; an assembler Root label does not mean Root authored or independently assessed this record.\",\n  \"supplemental_root_assessment_counted_as_independent\": false,\n  \"source\": {\n    \"algorithm\": 1,\n    \"sha256\": \"f1381784c66bb54164c9f5f5dc7f3c908fabb8dccd5065a8ce16732a9bfbb968\"\n  },\n  \"draft_manifest\": {\n    \"path\": \".build/phase278-current/reviews/prospective/f1381784c66bb54164c9f5f5dc7f3c908fabb8dccd5065a8ce16732a9bfbb968/manifest.json\",\n    \"bytes\": 90065,\n    \"sha256\": \"c1a71fa95dfdda1bf525c4878c6f234c82c78e0886cfb34961cef480569a493c\"\n  },\n  \"scope_decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"lane\": \"linux-cpu\",\n      \"scope\": \"supervised\",\n      \"draft_judgment\": {\n        \"path\": \".build/phase278-current/reviews/prospective/f1381784c66bb54164c9f5f5dc7f3c908fabb8dccd5065a8ce16732a9bfbb968/linux-cpu-supervised-judgment.json\",\n        \"bytes\": 86798,\n        \"sha256\": \"6045c55705d3f09bc7453349dfe50c968c60d116e6c49b3e826d40505a6e6967\"\n      },\n      \"decision\": \"APPROVE_PROSPECTIVE_CURRENT_SOURCE_UNCHANGED_FINITE_CRITERION\",\n      \"qualification_claim\": false,\n      \"recipe_unchanged\": false,\n      \"finite_quality_floors_unchanged\": true,\n      \"complete_lane_rows\": 55,\n      \"own_scientific_rows\": 11,\n      \"new_qualified_outcomes\": 0,\n      \"rationale\": [\n        \"I approve prospective applicability of this unchanged finite quality criterion to this exact scope. The human-approved canonical product PPO/mountain-car allocation changes150->300 iterations; the entire recipe is not unchanged. Quality floors, reference policies, strict initial-gain rules and every other allocation remain fixed. The longer schedule is an experimental allocation, not a demonstrated mechanical repair or convergence guarantee.\",\n        \"Exactly five original prescribed members must actually complete the frozen budget in original order. At least three SAME original members jointly satisfy authentic strict own-initial improvement and every applicable signal/reference predicate. Whole-five unchanged quality statistics retain all finite failures. Original served index0 independently satisfies its own learning/reference/quality, source/device/work/completion, exact-artifact Store admission and replay requirements.\",\n        \"No seed replacement, score filtering, imputation, best-checkpoint selection, row/cohort splice, automatic retry or further budget extension is authorized. Further evidence-led investigation if this one approved trial fails is authorized, with original failures and all started attempts retained.\",\n        \"Both current ordered55 vectors join the actual selected-package helper export: only the two PPO/mountain-car PlanIds change from Source8af, all110 report digests and108other whole objects remain exact. Eleven unchanged historical C2 policy source FILE pins are independently checked as FILEs, not a nonexistent exported projection vector. Current606 source raw pins match the frozen snapshot.\",\n        \"The recorded native build, selected-package compile and actual library joins are provenance evidence, distinct from scientific execution. My separate12657-byte independent review gives full compile/stream/binary/31-input/export/private-ID joins. The direct GHC command uses explicit package IDs, cleared source search and no-isrc fallback. The current repo-local plan/conf/static+dylib/local-package-cache/CLI/helper FILE pins were also rechecked in this assessment.\",\n        \"All historical C2/8af/605/9b primaries/support and failed attempts retain their original source, scope and outcomes. Backend engineering passes do not qualify rows; the full-unit failure, firstCFA85/86 failure, expected7/actual10 wrapper failure and inherited caller partial-head warning532bytes remain literal. Current final native engineering86/10/1/30 is technical evidence only.\",\n        \"This approves prospective review DATA, with zero current qualified outcomes. It provides no CPU55/Apple55 scientific result, model or producer origin, replay/Store admission, source journal, lane registration or phase completion. Actual complete current-source CPU55 qualification/admission and subsequent genuine Apple55 are separate obligations.\",\n        \"All11 supervised tuples and recipes remain Source8af-literal. Canonical base+[0..4], fixed heldout labels/targets and exact paired predicates remain. California retains100epochs,7000training/1000heldout,batch128/tail88,5500updates and700000examples per original seed1011..1015; fixed train-only normalization, reg-ord1 order and finalepoch100 remain unchanged. PPO300 changes the full55 lane context, not an SL recipe.\",\n        \"Classification requires strict exact final correct-count gain over authentic own initialization and final count >=max(heldout largest-class count+1, exact uniform-binomial alpha1/5000 critical count). Fresh integer binomial tails for1000examples and10/100/200classes give136/24/16; chosen tails are <=alpha and predecessor tails >alpha. Actual label imbalance can strengthen this rule.\",\n        \"The stated conditional all-five uniform-null bound is E[success-count]/3<=5/(5000*3)=1/3000 by Markov; across30 allocated cohorts the union bound is0.01. It needs independent uniform guesses over examples within each null seed, not seed independence. It covers neither adaptive repeated attempts, arbitrary neural initializers, mixed nulls, regression nor population accuracy.\",\n        \"Regression uses finite binary64 values as exact rationals: SSE(final)<SST and SSE(final)<SSE(actual initial) on identical heldout targets. SSE(c)=SST+n(c-targetMean)^2 shows strict best-heldout-constant dominance also beats any training-mean constant; the positive standardization scale cancels. The unchanged standardized-RMSE ceiling and whole-five/served0 checks remain additional restrictions, with no rounding/replay tolerance borrowed by strict learning comparisons.\",\n        \"Calibrated compact accuracy floors remain project restrictions, not independently established published-model parity. Tiny0.008 was selected after0.012; the exact200class1000example uniform control still requires at least16correct before any stronger majority condition. Seen-heldout adaptivity is explicitly acknowledged; later success is developmental evidence, not unseen-holdout replication.\"\n      ],\n      \"lane_limit\": \"Actual new-source CPU/oneDNN work and complete lane evidence remain required, with expressly scoped host ARS provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"lane\": \"linux-cpu\",\n      \"scope\": \"native\",\n      \"draft_judgment\": {\n        \"path\": \".build/phase278-current/reviews/prospective/f1381784c66bb54164c9f5f5dc7f3c908fabb8dccd5065a8ce16732a9bfbb968/linux-cpu-native-judgment.json\",\n        \"bytes\": 88661,\n        \"sha256\": \"9cbebf516afe3b433fab2a2a4bc16426033899a8de01ec940f954ecc9f2ff7b5\"\n      },\n      \"decision\": \"APPROVE_PROSPECTIVE_CURRENT_SOURCE_UNCH